itions.webp",description:"World-class eco-expeditions into the marine-rich waters off Land’s End where hundreds of wild humpback and gray whales breach, slap their tail flukes, and nurture newborn calves each winter.",address:"Plaza Bonita, Blvd. Paseo de la Marina 17, Centro, Marina, 23450 Cabo San Lucas, B.C.S., Mexico",location:"Plaza Bonita, Blvd. Paseo de la Marina 17, Centro, Marina, 23450 Cabo San Lucas, B.C.S., Mexico",directions:"https://maps.google.com/?q=Whale+Watch+Cabo+Marina+Cabo+San+Lucas",bestTime:"December 15 through April 15 (peak breach activity January–March); early morning tours offer glassy seas and clearest viewing.",website:"https://cabowhaletours.com",whyVisit:"Los Cabos is one of the premier whale sanctuaries on earth. Experienced marine biologists lead small-vessel expeditions equipped with specialized underwater hydrophones to hear haunting live whale songs.",rating:"4.8/5",tags:["Whale Watching","Wildlife","Eco-Tour","Bucket List"],category:"Wildlife Safari",cityRegion:"Cabo San Lucas",gpsLocation:"22.8856,-109.9125",bestSeason:"Dec 15 – Apr 15",estimatedDuration:"2.5 hours"},{name:"Wild Canyon Adventures (Desert ATVs, Ziplines & Suspension Bridge)",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/d2-wild-canyon-adventures-desert-atvs-ziplines-suspension-bridg.webp",description:"Adventure park on 115 private hectares in a canyon along the tourist corridor between Cabo San Lucas and San José del Cabo, offering ATV and UTV desert tours with a beachfront stop, ziplines, bungee, a giant swing, and a long hanging suspension bridge.",address:"Carretera Federal Libre Transpeninsular, Cabo San Lucas-San José del Cabo KM, Cabo, Real, 23405 San José del Cabo, B.C.S., Mexico",location:"Carretera Federal Libre Transpeninsular KM 18.5, Cabo Real, 23405 San José del Cabo, B.C.S., Mexico",directions:"https://maps.google.com/?q=Wild+Canyon+Adventures+Los+Cabos",bestTime:"Early morning (9:00 AM) to beat the desert midday heat and maximize combo acti